## 5. Generated model (A1/A2)

generated/types.ts: Account, Workspace, Board, Note, Card, Zone, Block, Edge, BoardContent,
CardEndpoint interfaces; AccountLocale, BlockType, BoardVisibility, DeleteZonePolicy, OperationType
enums; one payload interface per operation (CreateNotePayload ... UpdateBlockPayload,
GroupPayload/GroupInversePayload); the discriminated Operation union, the embedded OperationInverse
pair and the payload unions; CONTRACT_VERSION = "0.1.0".

generated/contract.h: `#pragma once`, `namespace project_air::contracts`, entity and payload structs
(std::string/double/bool, std::optional, std::vector), enum class enums, std::variant payload unions,
OperationInverse/Operation and `inline constexpr const char* kContractVersion = "0.1.0";`. It
compiles clean with `-std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`.

The generator reads schemas/ generically (entities, local `$defs`, operation payload `$defs`,
if/then discriminators, enums, optional/nullable fields, arrays, external `$ref`s) and special-cases
only the operation envelope composition (union + inverse pair + group recursion).

## 6. Parity harness (A3)

- test/parity/canonical.ts: reduce each fixture wrapper to
  `fixture|schema|valid|type|inverse|ids|fields|reason` (normalized reason, sorted unique UUID ids,
  sorted top-level fields); pure TypeScript, type-checked against the generated types.
- test/cpp/parity.cpp: self-written JSON reader (objects/arrays/strings/numbers/bools/null, escapes
  and `\u`), includes generated/contract.h, instantiates the generated operation model, prints the
  same canonical lines for the fixture paths given on the command line.
- test/parity.test.mjs: compiles the C++ program, runs it over all 77 relative fixture paths, and
  asserts both line sets are identical; also asserts 77 fixtures / 10 schemas / 45 invalid and that
  invalid fixtures keep valid=false and model fields in the description.

## 7. A4 - gates

board-check (run with no node_modules/), codegen (empty diff) and unit (with C++ parity) all exit 0
through gate.py; the three records are committed with the single P1-03 commit.

## 8. Known limits and open questions

- The C++ compiler version is not pinned in docs/versions.md (that file is outside this task's scope);
  the local Apple clang 21 is used and recorded here. A clang row should be added by the lead/P1-06.
- The parity canonical form is a normalized description (type, ids, inverse type, sorted fields,
  reason), not a full JSON Schema validation in C++; runtime validation is out of scope (P1-04/engine).
- The C++ payload union maps operation/inverse type to the payload structs generated from the
  schema `$defs`; the group payloads are recursive through std::vector, which compiles with the
  local compiler because std::vector supports incomplete element types.
- Generated files are committed and are checked by the codegen gate; a schema change requires
  `codegen` in the same task (AD-3).
